      "id": "piano.s7.l4",
      "title": "Root–fifth bass",
      "summary": "Play just the root and fifth of each chord for a light, open accompaniment.",
      "minutes": 11,
      "steps": [
        {
          "type": "explain",
          "title": "Root and fifth",
          "body": "A **root–fifth** accompaniment plays only the chord's **root** and its **fifth**, either together or one after the other. It leaves out the 3rd, so it sounds open and works under both major and minor melodies.\n\n- C: C3 + G3\n- F: F2 + C3\n- G: G2 + D3\n- Am: A2 + E3\n\nLH fingering: **5** on the root, **1** on the fifth. Alternating root (beat 1) and fifth (beat 3) gives a gentle \"oom–pah\" motion.",
